grund agent-setup-instructions — print the guided setup instructions for AI agents.

Usage:  grund agent-setup-instructions [--section NAME | --full]

With no flag it prints the core: the fresh-repository path, the contents, and
the adoption workflow. A fresh repository needs only that, or `grund init -h`.
The rest of the guide is ten reference sections, each printed on request.

Options:
  --section NAME  print one reference section
                  e.g. grund agent-setup-instructions --section rules
  --full          print the core, then every section: the whole guide at once
                  e.g. grund agent-setup-instructions --full | less

Sections, in --full order:
  config, citations, languages, members, scoped-guidance, schema, queries, editor, integrations, rules

The text is the Markdown shipped as `skills/grund-init/`: `SKILL.md` is the core
and `references/<name>.md` each section. It is embedded in the binary so installed
agents can discover the setup workflow without access to the source tree.

Exit:  0 instructions printed · 2 unknown section, unknown flag, or other CLI error.

Examples:
  grund agent-setup-instructions                  # the core: fresh path, contents, workflow
  grund agent-setup-instructions --section rules  # one reference section
  grund agent-setup-instructions --full | less    # the whole guide, a page at a time
